# HaloFormCraft — Project-Centric Migration Plan

> Migrating from `Hospital → Project → Form` to `Project → Hospital(s) → Form`

---

## ⚠️ Golden Rule: Form Lifecycle Is Untouched

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The **entire existing form creation, versioning, and publishing pipeline remains exactly as-is.** Nothing about how a form is created, how its schema/UI/logic is edited, how drafts become published versions, or how archived versions are handled will change.

The current form lifecycle that is **preserved without modification**:

```mermaid
graph LR
    A["Create Form"] --> B["FormVersion v1 (DRAFT)"]
    B --> C["Edit Schema / UI / Logic"]
    C --> D["Publish"]
    D --> E["v1 → PUBLISHED"]
    D --> F["v2 → new DRAFT"]
    E --> G["Patient fills form"]
    G --> H["Submission saved"]
```

**What stays the same:**
- `Form` model structure (title, description, created_by, is_active)
- `FormVersion` model (schema, ui_schema, logic_schema, status lifecycle: DRAFT → PUBLISHED → ARCHIVED)
- `Submission` model (form_version_id, patient_id, data, submitted_at)
- All existing form CRUD APIs (`POST /api/admin/forms`, `PUT .../versions/{id}`, `POST .../publish`)
- The Form Builder UI — drag-and-drop, field configuration, preview, conditional logic
- The Patient form-filling experience

**What is being added (layered on top):**
- `Project` and `Hospital` as **organizational wrappers** around existing forms
- A `project_id` FK on `Form` (nullable — existing forms still work without it)
- Metadata columns on `Submission` for tracking origin (`project_id`, `hospital_id`, `center_id`, `submitted_by`)
- New Admin UI pages **upstream** of the existing FormBuilder flow

---

## Current State Audit

| Layer | File(s) | Current State |
|---|---|---|
| **Models** | [models.py](file:///Users/apple/Desktop/form-creation/backend/models.py) | `User`, `Form`, `FormVersion`, `Submission` — **No Project or Hospital models exist** |
| **Schemas** | [schemas.py](file:///Users/apple/Desktop/form-creation/backend/schemas.py) | Pydantic schemas for Form, FormVersion, Submission only |
| **API** | [main.py](file:///Users/apple/Desktop/form-creation/backend/main.py) | Flat CRUD — forms are global, no scoping by project or hospital |
| **Admin UI** | [Dashboard.jsx](file:///Users/apple/Desktop/form-creation/admin-ui/src/pages/Dashboard.jsx), [FormBuilder.jsx](file:///Users/apple/Desktop/form-creation/admin-ui/src/pages/FormBuilder.jsx), [Responses.jsx](file:///Users/apple/Desktop/form-creation/admin-ui/src/pages/Responses.jsx) | 3 pages — Dashboard, Builder, Responses. No hierarchy UI |
| **Patient UI** | [App.jsx](file:///Users/apple/Desktop/form-creation/patient-ui/src/App.jsx) | Monolithic 42KB file. No site/project awareness |
| **Database** | [database.py](file:///Users/apple/Desktop/form-creation/backend/database.py) | SQLite, no foreign keys for projects/hospitals |

> [!WARNING]
> The current database (`forms.db`) has **no concept of Projects or Hospitals**. All forms and submissions are flat, global records. This migration adds organizational layers without modifying the core form engine.

---

## Phase 1: Backend — Database & Models
**Duration:** 2–3 days · **Risk:** Medium (schema migration)

### Goal
Introduce `Project` and `Hospital` as **new, standalone models**. Link them to the existing `Form` and `Submission` models via **nullable foreign keys** so that all existing data continues to work with zero changes.

> [!NOTE]
> The `Form`, `FormVersion`, and `Submission` models are **not structurally modified**. We are only adding optional FK columns alongside the existing fields.

### 1.1 New SQLAlchemy Models

Add to [models.py](file:///Users/apple/Desktop/form-creation/backend/models.py):

```python
class Project(Base):
    __tablename__ = "projects"
    id = Column(Integer, primary_key=True, index=True)
    name = Column(String, index=True)                    # "Longevity Pilot 2026"
    slug = Column(String, unique=True, index=True)        # "LON_2026"
    description = Column(String, nullable=True)
    created_by = Column(Integer, ForeignKey("users.id"))
    is_active = Column(Boolean, default=True)
    created_at = Column(DateTime(timezone=True), server_default=func.now())

    hospitals = relationship("Hospital", back_populates="project")
    forms = relationship("Form", back_populates="project")


class Hospital(Base):
    __tablename__ = "hospitals"
    id = Column(Integer, primary_key=True, index=True)
    name = Column(String, index=True)                     # "Baptist Hospital Bangalore"
    site_code = Column(String, unique=True, index=True)   # "BPA"
    project_id = Column(Integer, ForeignKey("projects.id"))
    address = Column(String, nullable=True)
    contact_info = Column(JSON, nullable=True)
    is_active = Column(Boolean, default=True)
    created_at = Column(DateTime(timezone=True), server_default=func.now())

    project = relationship("Project", back_populates="hospitals")
    submissions = relationship("Submission", back_populates="hospital")
```

### 1.2 Add Optional Columns to Existing Models (Non-Breaking)

These are **additive-only** changes. All existing columns and relationships remain untouched.

```diff
 # Form model — add OPTIONAL project_id FK (nullable, no impact on existing forms)
 class Form(Base):
     __tablename__ = "forms"
     # ALL existing columns stay exactly as-is:
     # id, title, description, created_by, is_active, created_at
     # ALL existing relationships stay exactly as-is:
     # versions = relationship("FormVersion", ...)
     ...
+    project_id = Column(Integer, ForeignKey("projects.id"), nullable=True)  # ← NEW, optional
+    project = relationship("Project", back_populates="forms")               # ← NEW

 # Submission model — add OPTIONAL metadata columns (nullable, no impact on existing submissions)
 class Submission(Base):
     __tablename__ = "submissions"
     # ALL existing columns stay exactly as-is:
     # id, form_version_id, patient_id, data, submitted_at
     # ALL existing relationships stay exactly as-is:
     # version = relationship("FormVersion", ...)
     ...
+    project_id = Column(Integer, ForeignKey("projects.id"), nullable=True)   # ← NEW, optional
+    hospital_id = Column(Integer, ForeignKey("hospitals.id"), nullable=True) # ← NEW, optional
+    center_id = Column(String, nullable=True)          # ← NEW, free-text for camps/sub-locations
+    submitted_by = Column(String, nullable=True)       # ← NEW, identifier of the data collector
+
+    hospital = relationship("Hospital", back_populates="submissions")       # ← NEW
```

> [!TIP]
> Because all new columns are `nullable=True`, the existing form creation, versioning, publishing, and submission flows continue to work **with zero code changes**. Forms without a project simply have `project_id = NULL`.

### 1.3 Migration Script

Create `backend/migrate.py` to handle existing data:

```python
"""
Migration script: assigns all existing forms/submissions to a
default 'General' project so nothing is orphaned.
"""
# 1. Create a default Project (slug: "GEN_DEFAULT")
# 2. UPDATE forms SET project_id = default_project.id WHERE project_id IS NULL
# 3. UPDATE submissions SET project_id = default_project.id WHERE project_id IS NULL
```

### 1.4 Deliverables

- [ ] `Project` model with slug, name, description, relationships
- [ ] `Hospital` model with site_code, project FK, contact info
- [ ] `Form.project_id` foreign key added
- [ ] `Submission` metadata columns added (`project_id`, `hospital_id`, `center_id`, `submitted_by`)
- [ ] `migrate.py` script — safe migration of existing data
- [ ] Verify with `python -c "from models import *; print('OK')"`

